## 2026-07-31 · declined · converting the green-release publish-triage rules to a check (#162)
- **Source:** the prose-to-checks sweep over this pack (#162, Refs #159).
- **Reason:** runtime, store-side state (`ITEM_NOT_UPDATABLE`) that leaves no repo artifact to
  check.
- **Actor:** the prose-to-checks sweep, merged by @missingbulb (owner).
[
  {
    "id": "tldr-release-root-version-align",
    "on_fail": "block",
    "failureMessage": "without the align step the repo-root package.json falls behind after every bump, and the version sharedConstants entry and cer/version-sync go blocking (#241, #245)",
    "scanFiles": ".github/workflows/chrome-extension-bump-version.yml",
    "checkEachFile": [
      {
        "require": "/([\"'])package\\.json\\1/",
        "what": "the bump job no longer writes the repo-root package.json; the \"Align the root package.json to the bumped version\" step is gone, so the next bump moves only the two release-config paths",
        "fix": "restore the align step from commit 2529b63 (PR #241); if a vendoring overwrite removed it, re-apply it rather than accept the stub, and say so on #245"
      }
    ]
  }
]

